    "assistant_text": "All 6 tests pass now.\n\nThe fix was in `settle()` (`src/ledger/engine.py:44-47`): it was computing the discount by summing `rules.discount_for(item.amount)` per line item, rounding each line to the nearest cent independently, then summing the rounded results. That's exactly what `test_exact_payment_settles_invoice`'s docstring called out: \"The discount is a property of the invoice, not of each line.\" Per-line rounding gave 105.66 total discount instead of 105.67, a one-cent-high `total_due` that no payment could exactly match.\n\nChanged it to compute the discount once on the invoice subtotal:\n\n```python\ndiscount = rules.discount_for(subtotal)\n```\n\nWith subtotal = 1428.00, `142800 \u00d7 0.074 = 10567.2` \u2192 rounds to 105.67, giving `total_due = 1428.00 \u2212 105.67 + 2.50 = 1324.83`, which matches the test's payment exactly.",
